# Project: Zed Raku language extension

A local (and eventually publishable) Zed extension providing real Raku
language support: tree-sitter syntax highlighting, indentation, bracket
matching, outline, text objects, and (optionally) RakuNavigator LSP.

Repo:      ~/Projects/zed-raku
Status:    IN PROGRESS (M1-M3 scaffolded, LSP wired; pending in-Zed install)
Owner:     johnm

---

## 1. Background / motivation

- Zed has no Raku (formerly Perl 6) support in the registry or built-ins.
- The only usable tree-sitter grammar is `acrion/tree-sitter-raku`, a fork of
  `tree-sitter-perl` with "initial" Raku adjustments (most notably hyphens in
  identifiers). It ships Helix queries.
- `tree-sitter-perl/zed-perl` is a complete, working Zed language extension
  and is our scaffolding reference.
- Until this lands, Raku files are approximated as Perl via `file_types` in
  `~/.dotfiles/zed/.config/zed/settings.json`.

## 2. Constraints / gotchas (verified 2026-09-19)

- [ ] **Extension id must not contain "zed"/"Zed"/"extension"** (Zed rule).
      Use id `raku`. The repo/dir may be called `zed-raku`.
- [ ] The grammar repo does **not** commit `src/parser.c`; must run
      `tree-sitter generate` (CLI 0.26.9 + Node 26 present).
- [ ] Zed dev extensions require **rustup** + wasm target
      (`wasm32-wasip1`). System Rust is installed but rustup is NOT.
- [ ] Grammar quality caps output: a few Raku-only constructs still
      mis-highlight/error: real junctions (`|`/`&` parse as bitwise ops),
      reduction/hyper/zip/cross metaoperators (`[+]`, `>>+<<`, `Z`, `X`),
      user-defined operators (`sub infix:<+>`), parameterized roles
      (`role R[::T]`), the `but` operator, and `q:to` heredocs.
      (We have patched most other gaps; see M1.)
- [ ] Grammar is licensed MIT; keep attribution.

## 3. Deliverables

- Local dev extension loaded in Zed via `zed: install dev extension`.
- Syntax highlighting for the Raku file set (see 5.2) + first-line shebang.
- Auto-indent, bracket matching, outline, text objects.
- (Stretch) RakuNavigator LSP integration.
- (Stretch) Published to the Zed extension registry.

## 4. Repo layout (target)

    zed-raku/
      .plan
