## 6. Test corpus

Collect representative files covering: scripts, modules (`.rakumod`), tests
(`.rakutest`), grammar (`regex`/`grammar`/`token`/`rule`), OO
(`class`/`role`/`method`/`multi`), `given/when`, junctions, twigils,
heredocs, POD, and `nqp`.

## 7. Risks

- Grammar covers Raku only superficially -> highlighting gaps.
- Zed query capture validation is stricter than Helix; unknown captures may
  be ignored or warn.
- rustup requirement adds setup friction; dev extensions build per machine.
- `file://` grammar URLs are machine-specific (dotfiles portability issue).

## 8. Interim approximation (done)

`~/.dotfiles/zed/.config/zed/settings.json` maps the Raku file set listed in
M2 to the existing **Perl** extension. This is intentionally temporary and
should be removed once this extension is installed, to avoid the Perl
extension claiming `.raku` etc.
